 "operation": "claim_ticket",
 "distinguishes": "Which signature entries bind a claim, under the bound template claim-gated names: an entry by the binder's address with scheme p256 does not, though it verifies; an entry with an explicit msg does not, and one with 32 zero bytes, which EIP-8141 refuses, does not either; two entries by the binder bind the claim if either is over the signature hash, in either order; and the holder's re-pricing, re-signed by the binder, is bound. A node that reads only the first entry resolved to the binder, or that accepts any scheme, fails here; the template, which scans every entry and reads the scheme first, gives the same verdict on each.",
 "source": "Transactions made with exp-frames' src/frametx at 85ee60d, its p256 signer included; tickets signed with Commonware at c18a6b9 over the 152-byte message; the bound template's 1185 bytes as the Hegota testnet serves them at block 493609. Each claim's validity was checked with Commonware, each secp256k1 binding with viem's recovery, and the p256 entry with noble's P256 verification, as EIP-8141's validate_signature at 258836f9 reads it, before the vectors were written.",
